<!-- graphkit:start -->
This repo has a local code graph at `graphify-out/` built by graphify (AST only, no data leaves the machine).

Before searching or opening files to answer a question about the codebase, run in the terminal:
- `graphify query "<question>"` for a scoped subgraph
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` for how two symbols connect
- `graphify explain "<symbol>"` for one symbol and its neighbours

Open only the files the graph names. Search the codebase directly when the graph has oriented you and you need exact lines, or when `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing. After changing code, run `graphify update .`.
<!-- graphkit:end -->
